      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "body-row",
          "type": "row",
          "props": {
            "gap": 5
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "body-col",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 12
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "s1-h",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The warning signs",
                    "headingLevel": 2
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s1-p1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Suspension problems tend to be reported late, because the change happens slowly enough that a driver adapts to it. These are the signs worth acting on.",
                    "width": "prose"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s1-list",
                  "type": "list",
                  "props": {
                    "heading": "What to check",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "columns": 2,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Uneven tire wear",
                        "desc": "Often the very first sign. When suspension components wear, the truck no longer distributes its weight evenly across the tires."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Rough ride quality",
                        "desc": "If the truck suddenly feels rougher, the suspension is no longer absorbing impact the way it should."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Leaning or sagging",
                        "desc": "A unit that sits low on one corner, or leans under load, is telling you something about springs, bushings or air springs."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Noise over bumps",
                        "desc": "Knocking or clunking over expansion joints points at worn bushings, pins or shock mounts."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2-h",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why catching it early matters",
                    "headingLevel": 2
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2-p1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The earlier a suspension problem is found, the easier and cheaper the repair usually is. The longer worn components run, the more strain they put on tires, steering and driveline components, so a single worn part turns into a list of them.",
                    "width": "prose"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s2-p2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "It also works in the other direction. Suspension condition and alignment are linked, so a truck that is going out of alignment repeatedly is often telling you about a suspension part rather than about the alignment itself.",
                    "width": "prose"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s3-h",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Getting it inspected",
                    "headingLevel": 2
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s3-p1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A suspension inspection is quick and is worth folding into scheduled service. Our parts departments stock components for all makes and models, and our technicians can replace what is worn and align the truck in the same visit so the new geometry holds.",
                    "width": "prose"
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
